! ============================================================================
!  Rerouter — Cisco IOS / IOS-XE (classic CLI) restricted parser view
! ============================================================================
!  Role-Based CLI Access "view" that limits the controller's SSH account to ONLY
!  the commands Rerouter actually issues:
!
!     reads      : show running-config, show ip route, show ipv6 route,
!                  show ip bgp, show interfaces, show version, show clock,
!                  terminal length
!     blackhole  : [no] ip route <net> <mask> Null0        (RTBH to Null0, IPv4)
!                  [no] ipv6 route <cidr> Null0            (RTBH to Null0, IPv6)
!     bgp session: router bgp <asn> ; [no] neighbor <ip> shutdown
!     bgp policy : router bgp <asn> ; [no] neighbor <ip> route-map <name> in|out
!                  [no] ip prefix-list <name> permit <cidr> ; clear ip bgp <ip> soft in|out
!     interface  : interface <if> ; [no] ip tcp adjust-mss <n> ; [no] shutdown
!
!  Everything else is denied by the view (fail-closed). This is defense-in-depth:
!  the controller ALSO only ever renders these commands from validated templates
!  with typed parameters (no free-text command path).
!
!  Replace <ENABLE_SECRET> and <VIEW_SECRET> before pasting. Tested shape for
!  IOS 15.x; verify command tokens on your image (`?` is your friend inside the
!  view: `parser view RRT-BGP` then `commands exec include ?`).
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- 1. one-time prerequisites (AAA + an enable secret to reach root view) ----
configure terminal
 aaa new-model
 aaa authentication login default local
 aaa authorization exec default local
 enable secret <ENABLE_SECRET>
end

! ---- 2. enter the root view (required to create/edit any view) ----
!  (interactive: run `enable view`, then supply <ENABLE_SECRET>)
enable view

! ---- 3. define the restricted view ----
configure terminal
parser view RRT-BGP
 secret <VIEW_SECRET>
 !
 ! -- reads the controller needs (Test SSH, verify, discovery, label parsing) --
 commands exec include terminal length 0
 commands exec include show clock
 commands exec include show version
 commands exec include show ip route
 commands exec include show ipv6 route
 commands exec include show ip bgp
 commands exec include show interfaces
 commands exec include show running-config
 !
 ! -- BGP soft-clear: activates bgp_advertise / bgp_route_map_set (exec-level) --
 commands exec include clear ip bgp
 !
 ! -- enter global configuration mode --
 commands exec include configure terminal
 !
 ! -- blackhole / null-route (RTBH to Null0), IPv4 + IPv6, in global config --
 commands configure include ip route
 commands configure include no ip route
 commands configure include ipv6 route
 commands configure include no ipv6 route
 !
 ! -- BGP advertise via outbound prefix-list --
 commands configure include ip prefix-list
 commands configure include no ip prefix-list
 !
 ! -- BGP session shut/no-shut + route-map change --
 commands configure include router bgp
 commands router include neighbor
 commands router include no neighbor
 !
 ! -- interface MSS clamp + shut/no-shut --
 commands configure include interface
 commands interface include ip tcp adjust-mss
 commands interface include no ip tcp adjust-mss
 commands interface include shutdown
 commands interface include no shutdown
 !
 ! -- OPTIONAL: uncomment so `show running-config` also reveals `network`
 !    statements, which announced-prefix discovery needs. NOTE: including it
 !    also lets the account edit network statements (slightly wider than
 !    shut/no-shut + Null0). Leave commented to keep the view minimal.
 ! commands router include network
end

! ============================================================================
!  Assigning the view to the controller's SSH account
! ============================================================================
!  IMPORTANT: IOS does NOT auto-assign a CLI view to a *locally*-authenticated
!  user — local login lands in the root/privilege context, and a non-interactive
!  SSH (publickey) session cannot run `enable view RRT-BGP` interactively.
!
!  Use ONE of:
!
!   (A) TACACS+ (recommended for an automated account): return the view on login
!       so it is applied with no interaction. Free-radius/ISE/ACS av-pair:
!           shell:cli-view-name=RRT-BGP
!       (with priv-lvl 15). This is the clean "priv 15 + view" setup.
!
!   (B) Local testing only: log in interactively and run
!           enable view RRT-BGP
!       then supply <VIEW_SECRET>. Good for verifying the command set, but not
!       usable by the controller's non-interactive session.
!
!  If you are local-only with no TACACS+, the controller-side allowlist (it only
!  ever sends the commands above) remains the enforcing control; tell us and we
!  can instead lower exactly these commands to a custom privilege level.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! ============================================================================
!  Granularity caveats (why the controller-side allowlist still matters)
! ============================================================================
!  * `commands configure include ip route` / `ipv6 route` permit ANY static
!    route, not only routes to Null0 — the Null0 keyword sits after the variable
!    net/mask, which a parser view cannot pin. The controller only ever emits
!    `... Null0`.
!  * `commands router include neighbor` permits ALL `neighbor` subcommands, not
!    only `shutdown` / `route-map` — the neighbor IP is a variable, so the view
!    cannot pin the trailing keyword. The controller only ever emits
!    `[no] neighbor <ip> shutdown` and `[no] neighbor <ip> route-map <name> in|out`.
!  * `commands configure include interface` + the `interface` sub-commands permit
!    `[no] shutdown` and `[no] ip tcp adjust-mss <n>` on ANY interface; the
!    controller only emits these against the interface named in the template.
!  * `commands configure include ip prefix-list` permits any prefix-list entry;
!    the controller only emits `[no] ip prefix-list <name> permit <cidr>`.
!  Pinning to the exact full command line requires TACACS+ command authorization
!  (regex per line) or the in-app allowlist — not local parser views.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
